{
  "fixture": "gfilter-picker",
  "version": 1,
  "encoding": {
    "model": "buildGlobalFilterPickerModel({sources, rows, query, expanded, mode, fieldType?, excludeDatabaseIds?, canEdit}) -> {flat, groups: [{databaseId, viewCount, fieldIds, more}], showFooter, empty}.",
    "sources": "The loaded source databases with their properties (primary first, then column order). Field types: 0 RichText, 1 Number, 2 DateTime, 3 SingleSelect, 4 MultiSelect, 5 Checkbox, 6 URL, 7 Checklist, 9 CreatedTime, 10 Relation, 11 Summary, 13 Time, 14 Media, 15 Person, 16 Rollup. Only global filter types count (Relation, Rollup, Formula, Time, Media, Summary and Translate do not); a source without one is left out.",
    "rows": "The dashboard rows, each a list of widgets {database_id, view_id}. Groups follow the order of first appearance; a database with no loaded source is skipped. viewCount is the number of widgets of the database.",
    "modes": "toolbar: flat (one group, no header) when exactly one source is listed, otherwise grouped; the footer ('Filter multiple sources') shows for writers (can_edit) with 2+ listed sources. multi: always grouped, no footer. add-another: grouped, only fields of fieldType, sources in excludeDatabaseIds left out, no footer.",
    "cutoff": "Without a query a flat list shows 8 fields and a group 5; more is the number of hidden fields, 0 once the group's databaseId is in expanded. A non-empty query (trimmed, compared with normalizeDashboardText as a substring of the field name) shows every match, hides groups without a match and sets more to 0. empty: no group is left."
  },
